<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    Auto Backup, for devices below API 31. See data_extraction_rules.xml for 31 and above;
    both files have to say the same thing or the rule only applies to half the fleet.

    kinex.identity.xml holds the recovery-phrase entropy, which is the whole account: the
    phrase, the private key, the device id and every synced session all derive from it. Two
    reasons it must not be backed up, and the second is the one that would actually bite:

      - it is the account, and an account key should not be sitting in a cloud backup;
      - it is encrypted with a key held in this device's Keystore, which is not backed up
        with it. A restored copy would be a file the app cannot decrypt, so backing it up
        does not even work — it produces an identity that reads as corrupt.

    The recovery phrase is how an account moves to a new phone. That is the whole point of
    there being one.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude
        domain="sharedpref"
        path="kinex.identity.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
